{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":6172,"ns":0,"title":"Cantor set","extract":"In mathematics, the Cantor set is a self-similar set of points lying on a single line segment that has a number of unintuitive properties. It was discovered in 1874 by Henry John Stephen Smith and mentioned by German mathematician Georg Cantor in 1883.","description":"Set of points on a line segment with certain topological properties","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}